>> title: Mole Poblano
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: chiles, chocolate, mexican, chicken, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: mole, mole sauce, pollo en mole
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, mexican-red-rice
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — a chile taken to smoke is bitter through the whole pot, and forty-five minutes of simmering only spreads it further
>> step.1: toast, soak 20 min
>> step.2: char 10 min
>> step.3: fry 8 min
>> step.4: toast 1 min
>> step.5: blend, sieve
>> step.6: simmer 45 min

Toast @dried ancho chiles{5}(stemmed and seeded; or half ancho, half mulato) and @dried pasilla chiles{4}(stemmed and seeded) in a dry #comal{} for ~{1%min} a side, then soak in hot water for ~{20%min}.

Char @tomatillos{4}(225 g; husked) on a dry #comal{} for ~{10%min}, turning until blackened in spots and slumped.

Fry @white onion{1%large}(sliced), @garlic{5%cloves}, @sliced almonds{1/3%cup}(35 g), @raisins{1/3%cup}(50 g), @sesame seeds{2%Tbs}, and @corn tortillas{2}(50 g; torn up) in @lard{1/3%cup}(75 g) over medium heat for ~{8%min}, until golden.

Toast @Mexican cinnamon{1%stick}(broken up) and @whole cloves{4} in @&(~1)nut mixture{} for ~{1%min}.

Blend @&(~4)soaked chiles{} with @&(~3)charred tomatillos{}, @&(~1)nut mixture{}, and @chicken stock{3%cups}(700 mL) until completely smooth, then push through a #sieve{}.

Simmer @&(~1)purée{} with @Mexican chocolate{2%oz}(55 g; chopped) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} for ~{45%min}, stirring often.
